# (the user, 2026-10-28) Sequence 2's octave moves with Motion: Sunrain (Sequence 2 at 0) at Motion 100 moves it an
# octave at a section change and back at the next; its page's Octave knob shows it (home + the shift), OCT- / OCT+
# light, the reader says it; the project keeps home. The hand wins: OCT- / OCT+ on its page, or its Octave knob, make
# what the knob shows, a step on, the new home, the shift gone (the times: this run's, deterministic)
wait 300
turn PRESET 5
wait 500
expect piece 5
spin K3 55
wait 300
expect par15 100
tap SEQ
wait 300
expect view 4
listen
# the first section change (~78 s): up an octave
wait 84000
expect section 3
expect s2shift 1
expect s2knob 1
expect par23 0
expect litbtn13 1
expect litbtn12 0
said Octave +1
shot shifted.png
# the next (~106 s): home
wait 25000
expect s2shift 0
expect s2knob 0
expect par23 0
expect litbtn13 0
expect litbtn12 0
# a later one (~140 s): down; OCT- makes -2 home, the shift gone
wait 40000
expect s2shift -1
expect s2knob -1
expect litbtn12 1
tap OCT-
wait 200
expect s2shift 0
expect par23 -2
expect s2knob -2
said SEQ 2 OCTAVE -2
expect litbtn12 1
# the next (~166 s): up from -2 (it can't go down); the Octave knob turned up makes the 0 it then shows home
wait 23000
expect s2shift 1
expect s2knob -1
expect par23 -2
spin K2 1
wait 200
expect s2shift 0
expect par23 0
expect s2knob 0
expect litbtn12 0
expect litbtn13 0
# (~196 s: from home, so it may roll at once) shifted again; Motion to 0 (HOME's KNOB 3): home at once
wait 30000
expect s2shift !=0
tap HOME
wait 300
spin K3 -100
wait 200
expect par15 0
expect s2shift 0
